{"uid":"83db36722093a8e9","name":"test_real_engine_live_then_container_gone","fullName":"tests.test_cli_steer_list#test_real_engine_live_then_container_gone","historyId":"feaf8e78c1631dc701eadbd2d8e0bf70","time":{"start":1791890046689,"stop":1791890048451,"duration":1762},"description":"The strongest test: steer a REAL engine from the CLI, watch `--list`\n    report it pending and then applied, confirm the hub says the same, then\n    stop the engine and assert `--list` still shows the same entries from the\n    run dir with the snapshot notice.\n\n    task 010 (B.4): STUB_HOLD_FILE/STUB_HOLD_PHASE=\"worker\" holds the first\n    worker iteration open instead of racing a real STUB_SLEEP window to\n    post the steer message while the run is still pending -- that held\n    iteration's own prompt was already built before the steer landed, so\n    it stays pending until we release the hold and a LATER iteration's\n    freshly-built prompt observes and applies it.\n\n    `ralphctl` itself runs in-process (task 003, requirement F) through\n    `_in_process_ralphctl`; the real subprocess boundary that remains is the\n    `ralphd-engine` child `live()` launches, unaffected by this change.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The strongest test: steer a REAL engine from the CLI, watch <code>--list</code><br />\nreport it pending and then applied, confirm the hub says the same, then<br />\nstop the engine and assert <code>--list</code> still shows the same entries from the<br />\nrun dir with the snapshot notice.</p>\n<pre><code>task 010 (B.4): STUB_HOLD_FILE/STUB_HOLD_PHASE=&quot;worker&quot; holds the first\nworker iteration open instead of racing a real STUB_SLEEP window to\npost the steer message while the run is still pending -- that held\niteration's own prompt was already built before the steer landed, so\nit stays pending until we release the hold and a LATER iteration's\nfreshly-built prompt observes and applies it.\n\n`ralphctl` itself runs in-process (task 003, requiremen